\clef sets the clef for an instrument.
It must be included inside a bar definition,
otherwise it will throw an error.
Its syntax is the following:

\clef bass

The avaiable clefs are bass, alto, treble and percussion
or its alias: perc.
This command must be used at the beginning of a melodic
line, like in the example below:

\bar clef-1 {
    \inst \clef bass c2 g,4 ees,
}

Once a clef is defined, it remains to this defined clef
until a new clef is set. This means that if the bar above
is executed, then the bar below will continue using the bass
clef for \inst.

\bar clef-2 {
    \inst c,4 d, ees,4. c,8
}
